---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import digitalProducts from '../data/digital-products.json';

const bookProduct = digitalProducts.find(p => p.id === 'power-without-the-panic');
const toolkitProduct = digitalProducts.find(p => p.id === 'solar-complete-toolkit-bundle');

const schema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Article",
  "headline": "The 2026 Levelized Cost of Electricity (LCOE) Index in Nigeria: Solar vs Petrol vs Diesel vs CNG vs Grid",
  "description": "Rigorous Levelized Cost of Electricity (LCOE) financial analysis in Nigeria based on IRENA and World Bank standards. Comparing solar kWh costs against ₦1,400/L petrol, ₦1,950/L diesel, ₦380–₦500/scm CNG, and Band A grid tariffs.",
  "author": {
    "@type": "Organization",
    "name": "Reid Caster Publishing"
  },
  "publisher": {
    "@type": "Organization",
    "name": "IbadanSolarHub",
    "url": "https://ibadansolarhub.com.ng"
  },
  "datePublished": "2026-09-17",
  "mainEntityOfPage": "https://ibadansolarhub.com.ng/nigeria-lcoe-solar-vs-fuel-cost-index"
};
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Nigeria LCOE Index 2026: Solar vs Petrol vs Diesel vs CNG vs Grid (Cost per kWh)"
  description="Official Nigerian Levelized Cost of Electricity (LCOE) benchmark. Compare true cost per kWh across Solar (₦150/kWh), Band A (₦219/kWh), CNG (₦315/kWh), Petrol (₦852/kWh), and Diesel (₦980/kWh)."
  schema={schema}
>
  {/* Hero Section */}
  <section class="bg-gradient-to-b from-slate-900 via-slate-800 to-slate-900 text-white py-14 md:py-20 border-b border-slate-800 relative overflow-hidden">
    <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-[radial-gradient(#f59e0b_1px,transparent_1px)] [background-size:24px_24px] opacity-10"></div>
    <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 relative z-10 text-center">
      <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3.5 py-1.5 bg-solar-500/10 text-solar-400 border border-solar-500/20 rounded-full text-xs font-semibold mb-4">
        📈 Academic & Energy Economics Benchmark
      </div>
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl md:text-5xl font-black tracking-tight leading-tight max-w-4xl mx-auto">
        The 2026 Nigerian Levelized Cost of Electricity <span class="text-solar-400">(LCOE) Index</span>
      </h1>
      <p class="text-base sm:text-lg text-slate-300 max-w-3xl mx-auto mt-4 leading-relaxed">
        What is the true, all-inclusive cost to produce 1 kilowatt-hour (1 kWh) of electricity in Nigeria? A complete empirical analysis comparing <strong>Solar PV + LiFePO4 Storage, Compressed Natural Gas (CNG), Petrol Generators, Diesel Plants, and Band A DISCO Tariffs</strong>.
      </p>
      
      <div class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap items-center justify-center gap-4 text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-400">
        <span>Methodology: <strong class="text-white">IRENA Renewable Costing Standard / World Bank LCOE Model</strong></span>
        <span>•</span>
        <span>Fuel Baselines: <strong class="text-white">PMS @ ₦1,400/L • AGO @ ₦1,950/L • CNG @ ₦380–₦500/Sm³</strong></span>
        <span>•</span>
        <span>Author: <strong class="text-white">Reid Caster Publishing</strong></span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-10 md:py-14">
    
    {/* Executive Summary Card */}
    <div class="bg-amber-500/10 border-2 border-solar-500/30 rounded-2xl p-6 md:p-8 mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-950 flex items-center gap-2 mb-3">
        ⚡ The Bottom-Line: True Cost Per Kilowatt-Hour (kWh) in Nigeria
      </h2>
      <p class="text-slate-800 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed">
        When upfront capital expenditures, fuel logistics, cylinder conversions, lubrication oil changes, top-end rebuilds, and equipment depreciation are amortized over a 10-year operating horizon:
        <br><br>
        • <strong>1. Solar PV + LiFePO4 Lithium:</strong> <strong class="text-emerald-800">₦145 – ₦175 per kWh</strong> (Lowest Lifetime Cost)<br>
        • <strong>2. Band A DISCO Grid:</strong> <strong>₦209.50 – ₦225 per kWh</strong> (+ inflation & VAT)<br>
        • <strong>3. CNG (Compressed Natural Gas @ ₦380–₦500/Sm³):</strong> <strong>₦300 – ₦380 per kWh</strong> (including conversion kit amortization & cylinder logistics)<br>
        • <strong>4. Petrol Generator (PMS @ ₦1,400/L):</strong> <strong>₦850 – ₦980 per kWh</strong><br>
        • <strong>5. Diesel Generator (AGO @ ₦1,800–₦2,100/L):</strong> <strong class="text-red-700">₦920 – ₦1,150 per kWh</strong>
        <br><br>
        <strong>Key Revelation:</strong> At recent dispensing rates of <strong>₦380 to ₦500 per Sm³</strong>, CNG generators now generate power at <strong>₦300–₦380/kWh</strong>—making CNG more expensive than Band A grid power (₦209.50) and <strong>more than double the lifetime cost of Solar PV (₦150/kWh)</strong>. While CNG offers substantial relief over petrol and diesel, Solar PV remains the uncontested lowest-cost energy source in Nigeria.
      </p>
    </div>

    {/* Section 1: Detailed 10-Year LCOE Comparison Table */}
    <div class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-4">
        1. 10-Year Levelized Cost of Electricity Breakdown
      </h2>
      <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-6">
        The table below models the 10-year total cost of ownership (TCO) required to deliver <strong>5,000 kWh annually</strong> (~13.7 kWh/day, equivalent to an active 3-bedroom residence, bakery, clinic, or tech office):
      </p>

      <div class="overflow-x-auto shadow-sm rounded-xl border border-slate-200 mb-8">
        <table class="w-full text-left text-xs sm:text-sm border-collapse bg-white">
          <thead class="bg-slate-900 text-white font-bold">
            <tr>
              <th class="p-3.5 border-b border-slate-800">Energy Source</th>
              <th class="p-3.5 border-b border-slate-800">Initial Setup & Equipment</th>
              <th class="p-3.5 border-b border-slate-800">10-Yr Fuel & Tariff Spend</th>
              <th class="p-3.5 border-b border-slate-800">10-Yr Maintenance & Parts</th>
              <th class="p-3.5 border-b border-slate-800">10-Yr Total Energy Cost</th>
              <th class="p-3.5 border-b border-slate-800 bg-solar-600 text-slate-950">Effective Cost / kWh</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody class="divide-y divide-slate-100 text-slate-700">
            {/* Solar PV Row */}
            <tr class="hover:bg-slate-50 bg-emerald-50/40 font-semibold text-slate-900">
              <td class="p-3.5">
                <strong class="text-emerald-900">LiFePO4 Solar System (3.5kVA / 5.12kWh)</strong><br>
                <span class="text-xs text-slate-500 font-normal">Tier-1 Mono Panels + High-Voltage Inverter</span>
              </td>
              <td class="p-3.5">₦3,100,000</td>
              <td class="p-3.5 text-emerald-700 font-bold">₦0 (100% Free Solar)</td>
              <td class="p-3.5">₦650,000 <span class="text-[11px] text-slate-400 block">(Year 6 inverter capacitor refresh)</span></td>
              <td class="p-3.5 font-bold text-emerald-900">₦3,750,000</td>
              <td class="p-3.5 font-black text-emerald-800 text-base bg-emerald-100">₦150 / kWh</td>
            </tr>

            {/* Band A Grid */}
            <tr class="hover:bg-slate-50">
              <td class="p-3.5">
                <strong>Band A DISCO Grid</strong><br>
                <span class="text-xs text-slate-500 font-normal">Subject to periodic NERC tariff indexation</span>
              </td>
              <td class="p-3.5">₦120,000 <span class="text-[11px] text-slate-400 block">(Meter & Connection)</span></td>
              <td class="p-3.5">₦10,475,000 <span class="text-[11px] text-slate-400 block">(@ ₦209.50/kWh baseline)</span></td>
              <td class="p-3.5">₦350,000 <span class="text-[11px] text-slate-400 block">(Estate transformer levies)</span></td>
              <td class="p-3.5 font-bold text-slate-900">₦10,945,000</td>
              <td class="p-3.5 font-bold text-slate-900 text-base">₦219 / kWh</td>
            </tr>

            {/* CNG Genset */}
            <tr class="hover:bg-slate-50 bg-blue-50/30">
              <td class="p-3.5">
                <strong class="text-blue-950">CNG Generator (Dedicated / Converted)</strong><br>
                <span class="text-xs text-slate-500 font-normal">Gas @ ₦440/Sm³ + Type-2 200-Bar Cylinder</span>
              </td>
              <td class="p-3.5">₦1,150,000 <span class="text-[11px] text-slate-400 block">(Genset + ₦650k CNG kit & tank)</span></td>
              <td class="p-3.5 text-blue-800 font-semibold">₦11,000,000 <span class="text-[11px] text-slate-400 block">(25,000 Sm³ natural gas @ ₦440)</span></td>
              <td class="p-3.5">₦2,850,000 <span class="text-[11px] text-slate-400 block">(Valves, plugs, cylinder hydro-tests)</span></td>
              <td class="p-3.5 font-bold text-blue-950">₦15,000,000</td>
              <td class="p-3.5 font-black text-blue-900 text-base bg-blue-100">₦300 – ₦380 / kWh</td>
            </tr>

            {/* Petrol Gen */}
            <tr class="hover:bg-slate-50 bg-amber-50/20">
              <td class="p-3.5">
                <strong>Petrol Generator (3.5kVA / 0.55L/kWh)</strong><br>
                <span class="text-xs text-slate-500 font-normal">PMS @ ₦1,400/L baseline</span>
              </td>
              <td class="p-3.5">₦480,000</td>
              <td class="p-3.5 text-red-700 font-bold">₦38,500,000 <span class="text-[11px] text-slate-400 block">(27,500 Litres PMS)</span></td>
              <td class="p-3.5">₦3,600,000 <span class="text-[11px] text-slate-400 block">(3x Gen replacements + oil)</span></td>
              <td class="p-3.5 font-bold text-red-900">₦42,580,000</td>
              <td class="p-3.5 font-black text-red-700 text-base bg-red-100">₦852 / kWh</td>
            </tr>

            {/* Diesel Gen */}
            <tr class="hover:bg-slate-50 bg-red-50/30">
              <td class="p-3.5">
                <strong class="text-red-950">Diesel Generator (7.5kVA / 0.35L/kWh)</strong><br>
                <span class="text-xs text-slate-500 font-normal">AGO @ ₦1,950/L retail market rate</span>
              </td>
              <td class="p-3.5">₦2,100,000</td>
              <td class="p-3.5 text-red-700 font-bold">₦34,125,000 <span class="text-[11px] text-slate-400 block">(17,500 Litres AGO)</span></td>
              <td class="p-3.5">₦5,200,000 <span class="text-[11px] text-slate-400 block">(Heavy 15W40 oil, filters, injectors)</span></td>
              <td class="p-3.5 font-bold text-red-900">₦41,425,000</td>
              <td class="p-3.5 font-black text-red-800 text-base bg-red-100">₦980 / kWh</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>

    {/* Section 2: Deep Dive into CNG (Compressed Natural Gas) */}
    <div class="bg-white rounded-2xl p-6 md:p-8 border border-slate-200 shadow-sm mb-12 space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-xl md:text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900">
        2. The Real Economics of CNG at ₦380 – ₦500 / Sm³
      </h2>
      <p class="text-slate-700 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed">
        With petrol at ₦1,400/L and diesel at ₦1,950–₦2,100/L, <strong>Compressed Natural Gas (CNG)</strong> has surged in popularity across commercial tricycles (Keke), ride-hailing cabs, inter-city trucks, and manufacturing facilities. However, with dispensing prices climbing to <strong>₦380 – ₦500 per Sm³</strong> at retail stations in major hubs, the economics reveal important trade-offs:
      </p>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-4 pt-2">
        <div class="bg-slate-50 p-4 rounded-xl border border-slate-200">
          <div class="text-blue-600 font-bold text-sm mb-1">⛽ Relief vs Petrol & Diesel</div>
          <p class="text-xs text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
            At ₦380–₦500/Sm³, CNG is still <strong>60% cheaper than petrol (₦852/kWh) and diesel (₦980/kWh)</strong>, providing essential survival margins for commercial transportation and factory shifts.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-slate-50 p-4 rounded-xl border border-slate-200">
          <div class="text-amber-600 font-bold text-sm mb-1">⚠️ The Logistics & Safety Burden</div>
          <p class="text-xs text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
            CNG requires transporting heavy 200-bar steel cascade cylinders to specialized mother/daughter dispensing stations (frequently facing long commercial queues) and paying for mandatory periodic cylinder recertification.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-slate-50 p-4 rounded-xl border border-slate-200">
          <div class="text-emerald-600 font-bold text-sm mb-1">☀️ Why Solar Crushes CNG for Homes</div>
          <p class="text-xs text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
            At <strong>₦150/kWh</strong>, Solar is <strong>more than 50% cheaper per kWh than CNG (₦300–₦380/kWh)</strong>, involves zero gas hauling trips, produces zero carbon monoxide emissions, and delivers silent 24/7 power.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    {/* Section 3: The Mathematical LCOE Formula */}
    <div class="bg-slate-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-6 md:p-8 mb-12 space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-xl md:text-2xl font-bold text-solar-400">
        3. Standard LCOE Calculation Methodology
      </h2>
      <p class="text-slate-300 text-sm leading-relaxed">
        The Levelized Cost of Electricity (LCOE) measures the net present value of the unit cost of electricity over the entire lifetime of a generating asset. We apply the standard formula codified by the <strong>International Renewable Energy Agency (IRENA)</strong>:
      </p>

      <div class="bg-slate-800 text-amber-300 font-mono text-xs sm:text-sm p-4 rounded-xl overflow-x-auto text-center border border-slate-700">
        LCOE = [ Initial Capex + ∑(O&M<sub>t</sub> + Fuel<sub>t</sub>) / (1 + r)<sup>t</sup> ] ÷ [ ∑ Energy_Generated<sub>t</sub> / (1 + r)<sup>t</sup> ]
      </div>

      <div class="text-xs text-slate-400 space-y-1.5 pt-2">
        <p>• <strong>Capex (I<sub>0</sub>):</strong> Includes turnkey inverter, LiFePO4 cells, tier-1 monocrystalline panels, DC/AC switchgear, and professional installation labor.</p>
        <p>• <strong>O&M (M<sub>t</sub>):</strong> Annual panel cleaning, terminal torque audits, and a designated mid-life inverter capacitor/motherboard refresh fund at Year 6.</p>
        <p>• <strong>Fuel (F<sub>t</sub>):</strong> Exactly ₦0.00 for Solar PV vs ₦1,400/L (PMS), ₦1,950/L (AGO), and ₦440/Sm³ (CNG).</p>
        <p>• <strong>Degradation Factor:</strong> Accounted at 0.55% annual panel output degradation and 1.8% annual battery capacity retention decay.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    {/* CTA to Calculator */}
    <div class="bg-gradient-to-r from-solar-500 to-amber-400 rounded-2xl p-8 text-slate-950 mb-12 flex flex-col md:flex-row items-center justify-between gap-6">
      <div>
        <h3 class="text-2xl font-black">Model Your Household's LCOE & Payback</h3>
        <p class="text-slate-900 text-sm mt-1 max-w-xl">
          Enter your monthly generator fuel and NEPA bill to calculate your exact breakeven month and 10-year cash savings vs solar.
        </p>
      </div>
      <a 
        href="/calculator"
        class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 bg-slate-950 hover:bg-slate-900 text-white font-bold px-6 py-3.5 rounded-xl shadow-lg transition text-sm whitespace-nowrap"
      >
        <span>Open Solar Calculator</span>
        <span>&rarr;</span>
      </a>
    </div>

    {/* Product Monetization Cards */}
    <div class="mb-14">
      <div class="text-center max-w-2xl mx-auto mb-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-slate-900">
          Official Nigerian Solar Publications
        </h2>
        <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 mt-1">
          Authored by <strong>Reid Caster Publishing</strong> to protect buyers from overpaying or buying bad hardware.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
        {bookProduct && (
          <div class="bg-white rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 p-6 shadow-sm flex flex-col justify-between">
            <div>
              <div class="inline-block px-2.5 py-1 bg-amber-100 text-amber-900 rounded-md text-xs font-bold mb-3">
                Flagship Ebook (30 Chapters)
              </div>
              <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">{bookProduct.title}</h3>
              <p class="text-xs text-slate-500 mt-1">Author: {bookProduct.author}</p>
              <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm mt-3 leading-relaxed">{bookProduct.description}</p>
            </div>
            <div class="mt-6 pt-4 border-t border-slate-100 flex items-center justify-between">
              <div>
                <span class="text-xs text-slate-400 block">Instant Download</span>
                <span class="text-2xl font-black text-slate-900">₦{bookProduct.priceNgn.toLocaleString()}</span>
              </div>
              <a
                href={bookProduct.checkoutUrl}
                target="_blank"
                rel="noopener noreferrer"
                class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 bg-solar-500 hover:bg-solar-600 text-slate-950 font-bold px-4 py-2.5 rounded-xl text-xs shadow transition"
              >
                Buy on Selar (₦{bookProduct.priceNgn.toLocaleString()})
              </a>
            </div>
          </div>
        )}

        {toolkitProduct && (
          <div class="bg-white rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 p-6 shadow-sm flex flex-col justify-between">
            <div>
              <div class="inline-block px-2.5 py-1 bg-blue-100 text-blue-900 rounded-md text-xs font-bold mb-3">
                Complete Tool Bundle (4-in-1)
              </div>
              <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">{toolkitProduct.title}</h3>
              <p class="text-xs text-slate-500 mt-1">Publisher: {toolkitProduct.author}</p>
              <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm mt-3 leading-relaxed">{toolkitProduct.description}</p>
            </div>
            <div class="mt-6 pt-4 border-t border-slate-100 flex items-center justify-between">
              <div>
                <span class="text-xs text-slate-400 block">Instant Excel & PDF Bundle</span>
                <span class="text-2xl font-black text-slate-900">₦{toolkitProduct.priceNgn.toLocaleString()}</span>
              </div>
              <a
                href={toolkitProduct.checkoutUrl}
                target="_blank"
                rel="noopener noreferrer"
                class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 bg-slate-900 hover:bg-slate-800 text-white font-bold px-4 py-2.5 rounded-xl text-xs shadow transition"
              >
                Get Toolkit (₦{toolkitProduct.priceNgn.toLocaleString()})
              </a>
            </div>
          </div>
        )}
      </div>
    </div>

    {/* Related Research Whitepapers Cross-Linking */}
    <div class="mb-14 bg-slate-50 p-6 sm:p-8 rounded-3xl border border-slate-200">
      <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 mb-4 flex items-center gap-2">
        <span>📚</span> Related Nigerian Energy Research Whitepapers
      </h3>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4 text-xs sm:text-sm">
        <a href="/band-a-tariff-vs-solar-index" class="p-4 bg-white rounded-xl border border-slate-200 hover:border-solar-400 transition">
          <div class="font-bold text-slate-900 mb-1">Band A vs Petrol Generator Payback Index</div>
          <div class="text-slate-500">Payback modeling under ₦1,400/L petrol and ₦209.50/kWh grid tariffs.</div>
        </a>
        <a href="/nigeria-battery-lifespan-tco-study" class="p-4 bg-white rounded-xl border border-slate-200 hover:border-solar-400 transition">
          <div class="font-bold text-slate-900 mb-1">Nigerian Battery Lifespan & 10-Yr TCO Study</div>
          <div class="text-slate-500">LiFePO4 vs AGM Dry Cell vs Tall Tubular heat degradation models.</div>
        </a>
        <a href="/nigeria-grid-collapse-feeder-reliability-report" class="p-4 bg-white rounded-xl border border-slate-200 hover:border-solar-400 transition">
          <div class="font-bold text-slate-900 mb-1">National Grid Collapse & Feeder Reliability Report</div>
          <div class="text-slate-500">11-year TCN collapse data (162 incidents) and Band A delivery deficits.</div>
        </a>
        <a href="/harmattan-monsoon-solar-derating-study" class="p-4 bg-white rounded-xl border border-slate-200 hover:border-solar-400 transition">
          <div class="font-bold text-slate-900 mb-1">Harmattan Soiling & Roof Heat Derating Study</div>
          <div class="text-slate-500">How 60°C Nigerian roofs and dust cut panel output by 12% to 25%.</div>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>

    {/* Citations & Data Sources */}
    <div class="bg-slate-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-slate-200 text-xs text-slate-500 space-y-2">
      <div class="font-bold text-slate-700 uppercase tracking-wider text-[11px]">Primary Citations & Standards:</div>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1">
        <li><strong>IRENA (International Renewable Energy Agency):</strong> <em>Renewable Power Generation Costs & Levelized Cost Methodologies</em>.</li>
        <li><strong>NERC (Nigerian Electricity Regulatory Commission):</strong> Multi-Year Tariff Order (MYTO) Band A-E Rate Schedules (2024–2026).</li>
        <li><strong>National Bureau of Statistics (NBS):</strong> Automotive Gas Oil (Diesel), PMS, and Natural Gas Price Watch reports (September 2026).</li>
        <li><strong>PCNGI (Presidential Compressed Natural Gas Initiative):</strong> Commercial gas conversion tariff & dispensing benchmarks.</li>
        <li><strong>Financial Modeling:</strong> Prepared by Reid Caster Publishing for IbadanSolarHub.com.ng.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

  </div>
</BaseLayout>
